---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const crumb = `<a href="${base}/">Home</a> › Editorial policy`;
---
<Base title="Editorial policy" description="How we source, check and correct what we publish." breadcrumb={crumb}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Original writing</h2>
      <p>
        Every article here is written for this site, from the underlying facts. We do not
        rewrite, summarise or translate other outlets' articles. Facts are not owned by
        anyone; the words used to report them are.
      </p>

      <h2>Two sources</h2>
      <p>
        A fact is published once it appears in at least two independent sources, or once
        it comes from the governing body itself. Where a result is recent enough that we
        cannot yet confirm it, the page says so rather than carrying a guess.
      </p>

      <h2>Data</h2>
      <p>
        Historical records are held as structured data and rendered directly onto the
        page, so the same figure cannot drift between two places. Each archive carries a
        note stating the last verified season.
      </p>

      <h2>Illustrations</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use club crests or press photography. Visuals are our own, including
        the colour badges that stand in for team identities.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Errors are corrected as soon as they are confirmed, and the correction is noted
        on the page. We would rather be visibly corrected than quietly wrong.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Advertising never influences what we cover or how. Any commercial relationship
        that could reasonably be seen to affect our coverage would be disclosed on the
        page it touches.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
